AB  - Endobronchial ultrasonography is a minimally invasive examination that offers new 
      opportunities for exploring the mediastinum. It reaches and characterizes 
      previously inaccessible lesions. Its relevance is largely supported by abundant 
      and compelling literature, which explains its increasing medical application and 
      the growing number of places offering it. This issue offers us an opportunity to 
      review the key points of this technique and to report on some of our findings.
