TI  - Endobronchial leiomyoma in children.
PG  - 136-9
AB  - Pulmonary leiomyomas are among the most rarely encountered benign tumors of the 
      lung in all age groups. The endobronchial origin and occurrence in children is 
      extremely rare for this tumor. The cases described reflect the efficacy of 
      bronchoscopy in the diagnosis and treatment of endobronchial leiomyoma 
      encountered in children.
