TI  - Endobronchial inflammatory pseudotumor: a case report.
PG  - 484-6
AB  - Inflammatory pseudotumor of the lung is a rare form of benign neoplasia and is 
      generally characterized by a solitary pulmonary nodule. The endobronchial 
      presentation is uncommon. Conservative surgery remains the treatment of choice, 
      and surgeons should always strive to achieve tumor-free margins due to the 
      possibility of local recidivism. This article reports the case of a 36-year-old 
      male patient with recurrent attacks of wheezing and cough. The patient underwent 
      successful bronchoplasty for the resection of an endobronchial inflammatory 
      pseudotumor.
