TI  - Endobronchial valve-induced pneumatocele: a case report.
PG  - 639-40
LID - 10.1055/s-0033-1344640 [doi]
AB  - We report a 75-year old female patient with advanced emphysema. After endoscopic 
      lung volume reduction with endobronchial valves (EBV), a huge pneumatocele has 
      occured and resolved spontaneously within a few weeks. Albeit rare, pneumatoceles 
      should be considered in patients with relapsing dyspnoe after EBV treatment.
