TI  - [Endobronchial brachytherapy: state of the art in 2013].
PG  - 162-5
LID - S1278-3218(13)00035-8 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.canrad.2013.01.008 [doi]
AB  - Endobronchial brachytherapy is an invasive technique, which allows localizing 
      radioactive sources at the tumour contact. Therefore, high doses are administered 
      to tumour while healthy tissues can be spared. Initially dedicated to a 
      palliative setting, improvements helped reaching 60 to 88% symptoms alleviation 
      and 30 to 100% of endoscopic macroscopic response. New diagnostic techniques and 
      early diagnosis extended the indications to a curative intent: endoluminal 
      primitive tumour, post radiation endobronchial recurrence, inoperable patients. 
      CT-based dosimetry is a keypoint to optimize treatment quality and to minimize 
      potential side effects, making this treatment a safe and efficient technique for 
      specific indications.
