TI  - Endobronchial lipoma: a rare cause of bronchial occlusion.
PG  - 263-4
AB  - Benign neoplasms of the endobronchial tree are uncommon, and among them lipomas 
      are the most uncommon. Endobronchial lipoma is histologically benign in character 
      but may cause bronchial obstruction. We describe a 47-year-old woman with an 
      endobronchial lipoma arising from the right main bronchus which was treated as 
      asthma for 4 years.
