TI  - Endobronchial granular cell tumor: a case report.
PG  - 29-35
LID - 10.3941/jrcr.v4i8.474 [doi]
AB  - Granular cell tumors (GCTs) are benign neoplasms that are most commonly found in 
      the head and neck region. We present a case of endobronchial granular cell tumor 
      presenting as hemoptysis in a 22-year-old African American female. Patient 
      subsequently underwent a right upper and middle lobectomy, and upon histologic 
      analysis was found to have GCT with borders impinging upon cartilage and adjacent 
      peribronchial lymph nodes.
