TI  - Endobronchial aspergillosis and actinomycosis associated with broncholithiasis.
PG  - 1144-6
AB  - Endobronchial aspergillosis or actinomycosis associated with broncholithiasis is 
      extremely rare. Here, we describe two cases of endobronchial aspergillosis and 
      actinomycosis associated with broncholithiasis. The patients underwent pulmonary 
      resection due to massive hemoptysis. These cases reveal that a bronchiolith can 
      potentially induce endobronchial fungal or bacterial infection, even in 
      immunocompetent patients.
