TI  - A case of endobronchial lipoma mimicking bronchial asthma.
PG  - 15-7
AB  - Endobronchial lipoma is a rare neoplasm of the tracheobronchial tree and it may 
      cause irreversible pulmonary damage due to recurrent pneumonia. Rarely, it may 
      mimic bronchial asthma. We present a 53-year-old woman with an endobronchial 
      lipoma, which had been treated as a bronchial asthma for four years. She also had 
      developed recurrent pneumonia three times.
