AB  - We report a middle aged smoker with recurrent pneumonia caused by endobronchial 
      actinomycosis secondary to a tooth aspiration. Unlike previously reported cases, 
      our patient was not chronically debilitated. The case suggests that a follow-up 
      bronchoscopy is beneficial after the initiation of antibiotic therapy for 
      endobronchial actinomycosis.
