TI  - Multiple endobronchial mass lesions due to sarcoidosis.
PG  - 190-2
AB  - Sarcoidosis is a systemic granulomatous disease that primarily affects the lung 
      and lymphatic systems of the body. The lungs are affected in over 90% of sarcoid 
      patients. Although paranchymal lung disease is more common, the airways may also 
      be involved. Bronchial mucosa is often affected in sarcoidosis, but endobronchial 
      mass lesions are very rare. We present a case with multiple endobronchial mass 
      lesions due to sarcoidosis.
