TI  - Surgical treatment of an endobronchial lipoma obstructing the right upper 
      bronchus: Imaging features with pathological correlation.
PG  - 1447-9
AB  - Endobronchial lipomas are rare benign unusual tumors of the respiratory tract. We 
      describe a 65-year-old Chinese man with a history of cough due to an 
      endobronchial tumor. The endobronchial biopsy was not excisional and was unable 
      to evaluate the whole tumor. Then the mass was successfully resected via a right 
      lateral thoracotomy. The histopathological diagnosis confirmed a benign lipoma 
      arising from the membranous trachea. His CT features and fiberoptic bronchoscopic 
      findings are shown along with the pathological results. In describing the 
      management of this case, we stress that the clinical treatment of such tumors 
      should be individualized according to the characteristics of each patient and 
      mass.
