TI  - Small cell lung cancer with endobronchial growth: A case report.
PG  - 553-555
AB  - The current study presents a rare case of small cell lung cancer (SCLC) with 
      endobronchial growth in a 68-year-old male. Chest CT scans revealed an 
      ill-defined mass in the upper lobe of the right lung, with ipsilateral 
      mediastinial lymph node swelling. An endobronchial polypoid tumor in the right B3 
      bronchus was located by bronchoscopic examination. The analysis of a biopsy 
      specimen obtained from the tumor resulted in a diagnosis of SCLC. Although 
      extremely rare, this case highlights the importance of considering a diagnosis of 
      SCLC in patients presenting with a pulmonary tumor adjacent to the bronchus, with 
      an endobronchial polypoid lesion.
