TI  - Hepatocellular carcinoma recurring as isolated endobronchial metastasis 8 years 
      after primary surgery.
PG  - 147-9
LID - 10.1097/RTI.0b013e3181972368 [doi]
AB  - Metastasis to the bronchus from an extrathoracic primary is a rare event. Most 
      endobronchial lesions are primary lung malignancies. Breast, colon, and kidney 
      are the most common primary tumors associated with endobronchial metastases. We 
      report a case of hepatocellular carcinoma that presented with hemoptysis due to 
      endobronchial metastasis 8 years after primary surgery. Indolent course of the 
      primary hepatocellular carcinoma and the solitary site of endobronchial 
      recurrence prompted a surgical resection of the endobronchial metastasis.
