TI  - Endobronchial schwannoma treated by rigid bronchoscopy with argon plasma 
      coagulation.
PG  - 174-7
LID - 10.4046/trd.2012.73.3.174 [doi]
AB  - Primary endobronchial schwannomas are extremely rare tumors that originate from 
      Schwann cells. We report a case of primary endobronchial schwannoma. A 
      44-year-old woman, without respiratory symptoms, was presented with a nodule in 
      the left main bronchus on her chest computed tomography scan. The nodule was 
      removed by a rigid bronchoscopy with argon plasma coagulation. Biopsy confirmed 
      the diagnosis of schwannoma. There was no recurrence during her 4-month 
      follow-up.
