TI  - Treatment of intractable pneumothorax with emphysema using endobronchial watanabe 
      spigots.
PG  - 226-9
LID - 10.5090/kjtcs.2013.46.3.226 [doi]
AB  - Prolonged air leakage is a major cause of morbidity in pneumothorax. When 
      conservative management is not effective, surgery should be performed. However, 
      surgery is not appropriate in patients with low pulmonary function. In these 
      patients, occlusion of the airway with endobronchial blockers may be attempted 
      under bronchoscopy. We treated two patients with prolonged air leakage using 
      endobronchial Watanabe spigots under fibrobronchoscopy.
