TI  - Mucoid impaction secondary to mucin-producing metastatic adenocarcinoma of the 
      cervix.
PG  - e201-3
LID - 10.1259/bjr/54252155 [doi]
AB  - Endobronchial metastases are an uncommon complication of malignant tumours. The 
      vast majority are secondary to carcinoma of the breast, colorectum and kidney, or 
      to melanoma. Occasionally, endobronchial tumours can result in partial or 
      complete bronchial obstruction. Here, we describe an uncommon case of 
      endobronchial metastasis of adenocarcinoma of the cervix causing mucoid impaction 
      owing to mucous production by the tumour cells.
