TI  - Endobronchial colorectal metastasis versus primary lung cancer: a tale of two 
      sleeve right upper lobectomies.
PG  - 379-81
LID - 10.1510/icvts.2009.207555 [doi]
AB  - Endobronchial metastasis from colorectal carcinoma is relatively uncommon whereas 
      primary bronchogenic carcinoma is more common. These two disease entities can 
      both appear to be similar clinically and radiographically. Palliative treatment 
      rather than a curative-intent anatomic resection is typically employed in the 
      setting of endobronchial metastatic disease. We compare two cases of patients 
      with a history of colorectal carcinoma with endobronchial lesions of which one 
      was truly a metastatic lesion.
