TI  - Endobronchial ultrasound guided needle aspiration of a paraspinal mass with prior 
      failed multiple diagnostic interventions: A case report and literature review.
PG  - 401-3
LID - 10.4103/0970-2113.142149 [doi]
AB  - The increasing frequency of tuberculosis (TB) in both developed and developing 
      countries has continued to make spinal TB an important health problem. The 
      present case report is about a patient who presented to us with progressive back 
      pain and paraspinal mass. We performed endobronchial ultrasound guided needle 
      aspiration from the paraspinal mass. The cytology showed granulomatous 
      inflammation suggestive of TB.
