TI  - Benign endobronchial granular cell tumor resulting in right middle lobe collapse.
PG  - 365-6
AB  - Granular cell tumors (GCTs) are generally benign neoplastic tumors of neural 
      origin that have little malignant potential. These tumors may occur in any 
      location, including the tracheobronchial tree. Although an endobronchial location 
      is believed to represent a small percentage of cases, GCTs should be included in 
      the differential considerations of any endobronchial lesions leading to airway 
      collapse.
