VI  - 21
IP  - 3
DP  - 2006 Aug
TI  - An unusual case of thymic carcinoma with endobronchial metastases manifesting as 
      centrilobular opacities.
PG  - 238-40
AB  - We report a case of a 75-year-old man having unusual manifestation of thymic 
      carcinoma associated with endobronchial metastases. To our knowledge, 
      endobronchial metastases secondary to thymic carcinoma has not been reported in 
      the literature. On high-resolution computed tomograms, the tree-in-bud 
      centrilobular opacities caused by metastatic cells accumulating within the small 
      bronchioles is indistinguishable from that caused by inflammatory process. Thus, 
      in patients with thymic carcinoma and persistent tree-in-bud centrilobular 
      opacities, endobronchial metastatic disease should be considered.
