TI  - Treatment of a transdiaphragmatic fistula with an endobronchial-blocking 
      catheter.
PG  - 1338-40
AB  - We report a case of a bronchosubphrenic fistula in a 59-year-old female following 
      hemicolectomy complicated by fecal peritonitis. The patient needed intubation and 
      positive-pressure ventilation, which caused a massive air leak. The fistula was 
      treated using an endobronchial blocking catheter in combination with antibiotic 
      treatment and drainage.
