TI  - Endobronchial myofibroblastic sarcoma presenting with hemoptysis in a patient 
      with a normal chest x-ray.
PG  - 314-5
AB  - Hemoptysis is an important symptom in clinical practice. The diagnosis of the 
      underlying cause is often difficult, particularly in patients presenting with a 
      normal chest x-ray. We report a case of hemoptysis with a normal chest x-ray due 
      to a rare endobronchial neoplasm: myofibroblastic sarcoma.
