TI  - Mucosal airway laceration secondary to endobronchial ultrasonography.
PG  - e31-2
AB  - Endobronchial ultrasound-guided transbronchial needle aspiration is becoming the 
      standard of care for mediastinal sampling to diagnose and stage lung cancer. It 
      is considered to be safe and rivals the gold standard, mediastinoscopy, in safety 
      and accuracy. The present article describes a mucosal airway laceration and 
      pneumothorax associated with the procedure.
