VI  - 59
IP  - 1
DP  - 2003 Feb
TI  - [Moderately abundant hemoptysis revealing endobronchial hamartochondroma].
PG  - 49-51
AB  - Hemoptysis is rarely the inaugural sign of endobronchial hamartoma. Abundance may 
      range from moderate to massive, and may be life-threatening. We report the case 
      of a 44-year-old woman who was referred to our center with moderate and 
      persistent hemoptysis. A left upper lobe lobectomy was performed. We discuss the 
      therapeutic options in such cases.
