DP  - 2013 Jun
TI  - The value of chest tomosynthesis in locating a ground glass nodule (GGN) during 
      endobronchial ultrasonography with a guide sheath: a case report.
PG  - E75-7
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2013.04.10 [doi]
AB  - A 74-year-old man was referred to our department for work-up of a pure ground 
      glass nodule (GGN) on computed tomography (CT). He was suspected to have lung 
      cancer by CT scan, but no lesion was visible on chest X-ray. Chest tomosynthesis 
      was performed before bronchoscopy, showing a clear GGN. We could not detect a 
      tumor signal on endobronchial ultrasonography so we relied on the chest 
      tomosynthesis image as a guide during transbronchial biopsy. The diagnosis of 
      adenocarcinoma was confirmed on histopathology. In this case, transbronchial 
      biopsy under the guidance of chest tomosynthesis was useful for the diagnosis of 
      GGN.
