TI  - Endobronchial valves for treatment of bronchopleural fistula.
PG  - 1129-31
AB  - Endobronchial valves have recently emerged as a possible alternative to lung 
      volume reduction surgery to treat incapacitating emphysema. The early experience 
      with placement of these valves has been shown to be safe, with short-term 
      improvements of quality of life in this patient population. We report a case in 
      which these valves were used to treat a patient with a persistent air leak.
