TI  - Endobronchial closure of postoperative bronchopleural fistula using vascular 
      occluding coils and n-butyl-2-cyanoacrylate.
PG  - 2174-6
AB  - We report herein 2 patients with intractable postoperative bronchopleural fistula 
      with empyema after lobectomy or subsegmentectomy. The patients underwent several 
      treatments including thoracotomy, but the fistula closure was not successful. 
      Finally, the bronchopleural fistula was successfully treated by endobronchial 
      closure using vascular occluding coils and n-butyl-2-cyanoacrylate (Histoacryl).
