IS  - 0021-5252 (Linking)
VI  - 62
IP  - 13
DP  - 2009 Dec
TI  - [Primary clear cell adenocarcinoma of the lung with endobronchial polypoid 
      growth: report of a case].
PG  - 1182-5
AB  - Clear cell adenocarcinoma with endobronchial polypoid growth of the lung is 
      extremely rare. A 65-year-old male with hemosputum was found to have an abnormal 
      shadow in the hilum of the left lung. Computed tomography of the chest revealed 
      that a heterogeneous mass occupied the lumen extending outside the upper lobe 
      bronchus of the left lung. By biopsy, the tumor was determined to be 
      adenocarcinoma. The patient underwent left pneumonectomy with mediastinal lymph 
      node dissection. Macroscopically, the tumor showed a polypoid growth along with 
      the bronchial tree. Microscopically, most of the tumor was composed of large 
      clear cells with partial glandular formation, indicating the tumor to be 
      adenocarcinoma Lymph node metastasis was seen in #5 and #12u. The lung cancer was 
      diagnosed as clear cell adenocarcinoma with endobronchial polypoid growth.
