DP  - 2014 Apr
TI  - Endobronchial cryotherapy facilitates end-stage treatment options in patients 
      with bronchial stenosis: A case series.
PG  - 120-3
LID - 10.4103/1817-1737.128861 [doi]
AB  - In keeping with international trends, lung cancer incidence and mortality are 
      increasing among the Irish population with many patients presenting with advanced 
      disease that excludes the potential for curative management. Consequently 
      palliative treatment options for this patient group are being increasingly 
      explored with various degrees of success. Endobronchial stenosis represents a 
      particularly challenging area of management among these patients and a number of 
      techniques have been described without the identification of a single gold 
      standard. We report our experience of the first time use of endobronchial 
      cryotherapy in Ireland with reference to a case series, including an example of 
      its use in the management of benign disease, in order to support patients with 
      borderline lung function and enable definitive palliative treatment.
