PMID- 15553037
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20041214
LR  - 20061115
IS  - 0021-5252 (Print)
IS  - 0021-5252 (Linking)
VI  - 57
IP  - 12
DP  - 2004 Nov
TI  - [Pulmonary embolectomy followed by lobectomy to treat for massive endobronchial 
      bleeding; report of a case].
PG  - 1153-6
AB  - We describe a case of successful pulmonary embolectomy that required lobectomy to 
      treat for endobronchial bleeding. Sixty-nine-year-old female got into shock 
      required CPR during rehabilitation after replacement of femur head. Her enhanced 
      computed tomography (CT) showed massive embolism in pulmonary artery. Emergency 
      embolectomy was performed under cardiopulmonary bypass (CPB). A videoscope was 
      employed to see inside the pulmonary artery. At the end of the CPB, endobronchial 
      bleeding occurred. The right bronchus was occluded by balloon and CPB was weaned. 
      The right lower lobectomy was done on the next day. She had got pyothorax by 
      methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA), and has recovered after 
      intravenous administration of antibiotics and continuous wash out of pleural 
      space by saline containing 0.02% povidon-iodine. Postoperative scan showed no 
      defects of blood flow and ventilation except resected lobe.
