TI  - Bronchial carcinosarcoma.
PG  - 26-31
LID - 10.3941/jrcr.v6i10.1049 [doi]
AB  - Carcinosarcoma is an uncommon mixed tumor of the lung. We present the case of a 
      65 year-old-male with cough and a right lower lobe radio-opacity who underwent 
      resection, showing a large endobronchial tumor with an epithelial component of 
      non-small cell carcinoma and malignant mesenchymal elements. The radiologic and 
      histopathologic features are reviewed with reference to relevant literature.
