TI  - Role of endobronchial and endoscopic ultrasound in pulmonary medicine.
PG  - 3-8
LID - 10.1159/000356921 [doi]
AB  - In the last decade, endobronchial ultrasound (EBUS) has evolved into an important 
      tool for diagnostic bronchoscopy in daily practice. EBUS has established as a 
      standard for the diagnosis of hilar or mediastinal lymphadenopathy, as a guidance 
      technique for peripheral pulmonary lesions and for the evaluation of tumor 
      involvement of the tracheobronchial wall or mediastinum. In the meantime, EBUS 
      has also taken a significant role in mediastinal staging in lung cancer patients. 
      However, EBUS plays not only a role in the diagnosis of malignancies, it is also 
      important for the diagnosis of benign disorders.
