AB  - We report a 6-year old girl with recurrent and non-resolving left-sided 
      "pneumonia" over a 3-year period who was diagnosed with an endobronchial 
      low-grade fibrosarcoma. This highlights the importance of considering underlying 
      localized airway obstruction in any case of clinically or radiologically atypical 
      pneumonia in a child and therefore the need for careful follow-up of all but the 
      most typical cases.
