TI  - Mycobacterium avium-intracellulare presenting as an endobronchial tumour due to 
      immune reconstitution inflammatory syndrome.
PG  - 441-2
LID - 10.1258/ijsa.2009.009370 [doi]
AB  - Mycobacterium avium-intracellulare (MAI) infection in an HIV-positive patient can 
      present shortly after starting antiretroviral therapy, as a result of immune 
      reconstitution inflammatory syndrome (IRIS). We report a case of a 33-year-old 
      woman where MAI presented as an endobronchial tumour due to IRIS. She responded 
      well to standard anti-MAI treatment (rifamycins, macrolide and ethambutol).
