VI  - 52
IP  - 18
DP  - 2013
TI  - Solitary extramedullary plasmacytoma presenting as an endobronchial mass.
PG  - 2113-6
AB  - Solitary extramedullary plasmacytoma (SEP) is a plasma cell neoplasm that 
      develops outside of the bone marrow. A solitary, exophytic growth in the airway 
      is an extremely rare presentation of SEP. We herein report a case of SEP 
      presenting as an endobronchial mass. The tumor was treated by rigid bronchoscopic 
      debulking followed by ablation using argon plasma coagulation. However, the tumor 
      could not be completely removed due to its wide base. Adjuvant radiotherapy was 
      administered as the curative therapy. A biopsy was performed on the resected 
      specimen and the diagnosis of plasmacytoma was thereby confirmed.
