TI  - Placing the tip of the endotracheal tube at the carina and passing the 
      endobronchial blocker through the Murphy eye may reduce the risk of blocker 
      retrograde dislodgement during one-lung anaesthesia in small children.
PG  - 690-3
LID - 10.1093/bja/aen264 [doi]
AB  - We present nine cases of one-lung anaesthesia in small children and infants in 
      which a novel technique was used to reduce the risk of endobronchial blocker 
      retrograde dislodgement. The technique involved threading the stem of the blocker 
      through the Murphy eye of the endotracheal tube (ETT) and deliberately passing 
      the tip of the ETT all the way to the carina. The tip of the ETT blocked any 
      retrograde movement of the blocker.
