DP  - 2014 Jul
TI  - Narrow-band imaging bronchoscopy in tracheobronchial amyloidosis.
PG  - 267-70
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0000000000000083 [doi]
AB  - Primary tracheobronchial amyloidosis (TBA) is a rare disease characterized by 
      extracellular focal or diffuse submucosal deposits of amyloid proteins. Various 
      types of endobronchial lesions have been described in TBA when bronchoscopy is 
      performed using white light. Narrow-band imaging bronchoscopy has been mainly 
      employed for detecting preneoplastic and neoplastic endobronchial lesions as it 
      provides more detailed images of the microvasculature reflective of an altered 
      angiogenesis process. Here, we describe bronchoscopic findings with white light 
      and narrow-band imaging in 2 patients presenting with central airway obstructive 
      disease later confirmed as having primary TBA.
