TI  - An Endobronchial Inflammatory Myofibroblastic Tumor Treated by Modified Left 
      One-stoma-type Carinoplasty.
PG  - 263-6
LID - 10.5090/kjtcs.2012.45.4.263 [doi]
AB  - Endobronchial inflammatory myofibroblastic tumor is a rare primary lung disease. 
      A 39-year-old woman with dyspnea and a productive cough underwent complete 
      surgical resection of a small-sized inflammatory myofibroblastic tumor that 
      invaded the left main bronchus and the carina with lung-saving modified left 
      one-stoma-type carinoplasty. We report this case with a review of literature.
