PMID- 24736536
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20140725
LR  - 20141120
IS  - 0023-1207 (Print)
IS  - 0023-1207 (Linking)
IP  - 2
DP  - 2014
TI  - [The effectiveness of the valve bronchial occlusion in case of bronchopleural 
      fistulas].
PG  - 22-4
AB  - The experience of endobronchial valve «Medlung" installation in 24 patients with 
      bronchopleural fistula was summarized in the article. In 18 (75%) patients the 
      cause of bronchopleural fistula was purulent - destructive processes in the 
      lungs, including the associated trauma in 4 (22.2%) patients, pneumonia in 14 
      (77.8%) patients. In 3 (12.5%) cases the cause of the bronchopleural fistula was 
      the lung tumors of different localization and in 3 (12.5%) cases - idiopathic 
      pulmonary fibrosis. Reasonable use of endobronchial valve in patients with 
      bronchopleural fistula provides a persistent separation of the fistula and lets 
      to avoid extensive, traumatic operations.
