TI  - Endobronchial metallic foreign body in a Nigerian child: management difficulties 
      and the need for caution: a case report.
PG  - 7766
LID - 10.4076/1757-1626-2-7766 [doi]
LID - 7766
AB  - INTRODUCTION: Endobronchial metallic foreign bodies are serious injuries best 
      treated by rigid bronchoscopy as quickly as possible to avoid life threatening 
      respiratory sequelae. CASE PRESENTATION: We report the case of a 13-year-old male 
      Nigerian child of the tangale ethnic group who aspirated a metallic foreign body, 
      highlighting the "difficulties" encountered in managing this patient. 
      CONCLUSIONS: There is a need to adequately equip our hospitals for the management 
      of this otherwise straight forward case and alleviate the sufferings of our 
      people. Parents and guardians should exercise caution in the handling of their 
      children/wards.
