DP  - 2011 Mar
TI  - X-linked agammaglobulinemia complicated with endobronchial tuberculosis.
PG  - 466-8
LID - 10.1111/j.1651-2227.2010.02071.x [doi]
AB  - AIM: We report a case of X-linked agammaglobulinemia complicated with 
      endobronchial tuberculosis. METHODS: We observed the patient's clinical course 
      and analysed his data retrospectively. RESULTS: Interestingly, the T-cell 
      proliferation activity in this patient was intact, and the CD4-positive T cells 
      produced interferon gamma. However, the result of the quantiferon alpha-2b test 
      was negative. CONCLUSION: The findings of this case suggest that the quantiferon 
      alpha-2b test may not be diagnostic for tuberculosis not only in patients with 
      T-cell disorders but also in cases with B-cell deficiencies such as X-linked 
      agammaglobulinemia.
