TI  - Rescue therapy using an endobronchial valve and digital air leak monitoring in 
      Invasive Pulmonary Aspergillosis.
PG  - 27-9
LID - 10.1016/j.rmcr.2014.12.001 [doi]
AB  - In this case report, we describe the utilisation of two recently developed 
      technologies for the successful management of a persistent air leak (PAL) in a 
      critically ill patient in whom cardiothoracic surgical intervention was not 
      possible. We report the case of a young leukaemic woman with a PAL complicating 
      Invasive Pulmonary Aspergillosis (IPA), who was effectively managed using an 
      Endobronchial Valve, supplemented by objective, digital air leak data provided by 
      a Thopaz(®) device (Medela, Switzerland).
