TI  - Endobronchial ultrasound: A new innovation in bronchoscopy.
PG  - 17-21
LID - 10.4103/0970-2113.45199 [doi]
AB  - Technical development in last two decades has made it possible for pulmonologists 
      to do endobronchial ultrasound (EBUS). With EBUS mini-probe, the multilayered 
      structure of the tracheobronchial wall can be analyzed better than any other 
      imaging modality. Instead of fluoroscopic guided biopsy, EBUS can be used to 
      biopsy peripheral lesions. EBUS-transbronchial needle aspiration has proved 
      valuable for mediastinal lymph node staging of lung cancer. Studies have shown 
      that EBUS is cost-effective as it reduces the need for more morbid and costly 
      invasive procedure like mediastinoscopy or thoracotomy. Prospective studies are 
      needed in India to see how EBUS will help in populations with high prevalence of 
      tuberculosis.
