TI  - Endoscopic and endobronchial ultrasound real-time fine-needle aspiration for 
      staging of the mediastinum in lung cancer.
PG  - 2020-2
AB  - Mediastinal lymph node metastases in patients with non-small cell lung cancer are 
      a critical determinant of operability. Mediastinoscopy is invasive, requires 
      general anesthesia, and carries appreciable morbidity. The development of 
      minimally invasive techniques for the pathologic staging of lung cancer is 
      important. We report a one-stop minimally invasive method for the pathologic 
      diagnosis and staging of the majority of the mediastinum under conscious sedation 
      using a novel prototype endobronchial ultrasound probe with a real-time 
      fine-needle aspiration (FNA) facility in combination with conventional endoscopic 
      ultrasound FNA.
