TI  - An endobronchial inflammatory myofibroblastic tumor in a 10-yr-old child after 
      allogeneic hematopoietic cell transplantation.
PG  - E165-8
LID - 10.1111/petr.12275 [doi]
AB  - IMTs belong to the group of soft tissue tumor and could occur at any anatomical 
      site; however, the causes and growth feature remain unclear. This case report 
      documents a 10-yr-old male suffering from slowly developing dyspnea on exertion 
      and cough around seven months post-HCT. He was diagnosed with an endobronchial 
      tumor based on imaging, and histology confirmed ALK-positive submucosal 
      spindle-shaped cells with infiltrative cells, compatible with IMT. We should be 
      aware that IMT is a potential complication of pediatric allogeneic HCT and can 
      cause sudden airway obstruction.
