DP  - 2006 Oct
TI  - Bronchial infiltration with diffuse large B-cell lymphoma.
PG  - 1319-22
AB  - Non-Hodgkin's lymphoma (NHL) refers to a heterogeneous group of 
      lymphoproliferative diseases with a diversity of clinical courses, including 
      involvement in another organs. NHL frequently involves the thoracic structures, 
      and particularly the mediastinum and lung parenchyma. Several clinical reports 
      have described bronchial-associated lymphoid tissue (BALT) lymphoma as an 
      endobronchial lesion, but endobronchial infiltration with diffuse large B-cell 
      lymphoma is extremely rare. Here, we provide the first report of this condition 
      confirmed by a histopathological study and the presence of an immunoglobulin 
      heavy chain (IgH) gene rearrangement detected by a polymerase chain reaction 
      (PCR).
