DP  - 2010
TI  - Restaging by endobronchial ultrasound-guided transbronchial needle aspiration in 
      patients with inoperable advanced lung cancer.
PG  - 787-90
AB  - We present two cases of inoperable advanced lung cancer in which the main lesions 
      were mediastinal lymph nodes detected with positive positron emission tomography 
      (PET). Drug therapy was very effective, and post-treatment PET results were 
      negative. Restaging by endobronchial ultrasound-guided transbronchial needle 
      aspiration (EBUS-TBNA) was performed on the mediastinal lymph nodes with a short 
      axis < or = 10 mm measured by computed tomography (CT). Cancer cells were 
      detected, which helped determine the therapeutic strategy. Re-evaluation of 
      mediastinal lymph nodes using EBUS-TBNA appears to be useful, even among patients 
      with inoperable advanced lung cancer.
