VI  - 145
IP  - 29
DP  - 2004 Jul 18
TI  - [Endobronchial ultrasonography in postintubation tracheal stenosis].
PG  - 1507-10
AB  - INTRODUCTION: The correct evaluation of the tracheal wall's structure is 
      necessary for the management of postintubation tracheal stenosis (PTS). 
      Endobronchial ultrasonography (EBUS) is suitable for visualisation of layers of 
      the tracheal wall and the assessment of cartilages' damage. AIM: The authors 
      assessed the usefulness of EBUS in the anatomical characterization of PTS and in 
      the decision making in its therapy. PATIENTS, METHODS: Between March 2002, and 
      September 2003, 22 patients with PTS were examined by bronchoscopy together with 
      EBUS. RESULTS: 13 patients had complex stenosis and from them destruction of 
      tracheal cartilage was demonstrated in 5 patients. Of them bronchoscopic 
      intervention resulted in only short term symptom free period in 3 patients. 
      CONCLUSION: The destruction of tracheal cartilage detected by EBUS might be an 
      indication for an early surgical intervention. According to author's results EBUS 
      can be a useful method in evaluation of PTS.
