TI  - [Observation of the lungs using ultrasonography].
PG  - 962-8
AB  - The three ways to observe the lungs using ultrasonography are transthoracic 
      echography, transesophageal echography and endobronchial ultrasonography. All 
      methods have their own advantages. Consolidation and pleural effusion are 
      evaluated with transthoracic echography and transesophageal echography. The 
      advent of comet-tail artifact observation made the transthoracic echography 
      worthwhile.
