TI  - Atypical carcinoid tumour.
PG  - 213-5
AB  - Carcinoid tumour is a rare entity accounting for less than two percent of 
      bronchial neoplasms. The clinical presentation is highly variable and rarely, it 
      may present as a solitary pulmonary nodule. More offten, it presents as a central 
      endobronchial tumour. The peripheral type of carcinoid tumour is relatively rare.
