TI  - Endobronchial fibroepithelial polyp.
PG  - 56-8
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e3181cdefc9 [doi]
AB  - Benign polypoid lesions are an uncommon finding on bronchoscopic examination. The 
      histopathologic fibroepithelial subtype is very rare in this location. In this 
      report, we describe a 77-year-old man diagnosed with a fibroepithelial polyp 
      located at the bifurcation of the left main bronchus; this was completely removed 
      using flexible bronchoscope.
