AB  - A fiberoptic examination is recommended at the end of lung transplantation for 
      bronchial toilet and to check the bronchial anastomoses. This procedure permitted 
      detection of a 10 × 4-mm piece of plastic of unknown origin in the left lingular 
      bronchus and suggests that bronchoscopy should be performed before implanting the 
      transplanted lung.
