TI  - Tracheal glomus tumor successfully resected with rigid bronchoscopy: a case 
      report.
PG  - 1065-7
LID - 10.1097/JTO.0b013e318183af45 [doi]
AB  - Glomus tumor of the trachea is a rare disease. A glomus tumor of the trachea in a 
      70-year-old man is described. The tumor was successfully excised with rigid 
      bronchoscopy. Twenty-four months after treatment there remains no evidence of 
      endobronchial regrowth at bronchoscopy or imaging studies. Histologic features 
      and treatment are discussed.
