TI  - Pulmonary atelectasis from compression of the left main bronchus by an aortic 
      aneurysm.
PG  - e247-9
AB  - Pulmonary atelectasis may be caused by endobronchial lesions or by extrinsic 
      compression of the bronchus. However, lung collapse due to compression from a 
      thoracic aneurysm is uncommon. We report a 76-year-old hypertensive female 
      patient who has pulmonary atelectasis due to an extrinsic compression from a 
      descending thoracic aortic aneurysm, and discuss possible treatment options.
