AB  - Unusual location and presentation of hydatid cyst disease in the thorax requires 
      careful consideration with respect to clinical approach and therapy. In this 
      pictorial essay, we present imaging findings and describe treatment of thoracic 
      hydatid cysts in patients with lung, mediastinal, chest wall, cardiac, 
      endobronchial, pulmonary artery, and diaphragmatic involvement. A review of the 
      literature is also included.
