PMID- 24443340
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20150106
LR  - 20211021
IS  - 1757-790X (Electronic)
IS  - 1757-790X (Linking)
VI  - 2014
DP  - 2014 Jan 17
TI  - Atypical presentation of typical carcinoid.
LID - 10.1136/bcr-2013-202870 [doi]
LID - bcr2013202870
AB  - Bronchial carcinoid tumours can present with symptoms of distal airway 
      obstruction, local airway irritation or bleeding due to hypervascularity. 
      Presentation with a spontaneous pneumothorax (SP) is rare. We present a case of 
      typical endobronchial carcinoid tumour that presented with a SP. We explored the 
      possible mechanisms of this rare presentation, especially the check-valve 
      mechanism of airway obstruction, which was evident during the fiberoptic 
      bronchoscopic examination.
