TI  - Radiotherapy for a pulmonary aspergilloma complicating p-ANCA positive small 
      vessel vasculitis.
PG  - e215-7
AB  - Life-threatening haemoptysis may complicate aspergillomas within pre-existing 
      lung cavities. Treatment options have included lung resection, pulmonary or 
      bronchial artery embolisation and antifungal therapy administered either 
      systemically or by endobronchial or percutaneous instillation. We present a case 
      of aspergilloma complicating small vessel vasculitis, and its successful 
      treatment using radiotherapy.
