TI  - An approach to tracheostomy in a patient with an expandable metallic tracheal 
      stent.
PG  - 731-2
AB  - With increasing use of expandable metallic stents to manage patients with a 
      variety of endobronchial pathologies, some will have a subsequent need for 
      tracheostomy insertion. We describe a successful technique to insert a 
      tracheostomy using rigid and fibre-optic bronchoscopy in a patient who had an 8 
      cm expandable metallic tracheal stent deployed previously on account of 
      tracheomalacia.
