TI  - Central airway obstruction caused by a peripheral hamartoma.
PG  - 395-8
AB  - We report the first case of a hamartoma, arising from peripheral lung tissue, 
      which extended proximally over several decades to occlude the large airways. The 
      patient's symptoms were originally attributed to asthma and the correct diagnosis 
      was only made when she developed life-threatening airway obstruction. The 
      endobronchial component of the hamartoma was debulked with urgent laser therapy, 
      while the peripheral base of the tumour was resected by elective right middle 
      lobectomy.
