TI  - Nocardia cyriacigeorgica intracavitary lung colonization: first report of an 
      actinomycetic rather than fungal ball in bronchiectasis.
LID - 10.1136/bcr-2012-007900 [doi]
LID - bcr2012007900
AB  - We report the first case of an isolated endobronchial mass caused by Nocardia 
      cyriacigeorgica in an immunocompetent patient with a history of lung surgery; 
      this is a rare presentation of an emerging opportunistic pathogen. The infection 
      was successfully eradicated by surgery. Microbiologists and clinicians should pay 
      more attention to this group of filamentous bacteria, which in the past have 
      often been neglected by medical personnel.
