VI  - 13
DP  - 2014
TI  - Argon plasma coagulation in the management of uncovered tracheal stent fracture.
PG  - 37-8
LID - 10.1016/j.rmcr.2014.09.004 [doi]
AB  - Endotracheal and endobronchial stenting, particularly with uncovered stents, can 
      be complicated by stent fracture, granulation tissue formation, direct airway 
      injury, and airway obstruction. While stent removal is possible, it can result in 
      significant complications and long-term benefit is not guaranteed. Argon plasma 
      coagulation can be employed to trim fractured stent fragments and remove 
      granulation tissue simultaneously. In this manuscript, we report a case and 
      describe our experience with using this technique.
