TI  - A case of haemoptysis due to endobrnchial fibroma, a rare benign tumour of lung.
PG  - 25-7
LID - 10.4103/0970-2113.44135 [doi]
AB  - A case of recurrent haemoptysis due to fibroma is described in a 55 years old 
      male patient. Clinical examination revealed anaemia and bilateral basal 
      crepitations. Chest X - ray showed no abnormality. Bronchoscopy revealed polypoid 
      fibroma in left main bronchus. It was removed bonchoscopically with no recurrence 
      during 12 months follow up.
