TI  - Primary pulmonary malignant melanoma presenting with haemoptysis.
PG  - 219-21
AB  - Primary pulmonary melanoma is a rare disease, and only 20 cases have been 
      published previously in the English literature. A 44-year-old woman presented 
      initially with haemoptysis, and a chest roentgenogram showed a single lung mass. 
      The diagnosis of primary pulmonary melanoma necessitates reliance on both 
      clinical and histological criteria. The image of endobronchial ultrasonography 
      (EBUS) in our case was not distinct from the image of lung cancer.
