TI  - Primary pleomorphic sarcoma of lung--11 year survival.
PG  - 44-7
AB  - Primary sarcomas of the lung are uncommon, potentially aggressive neoplasms that 
      need to be distinguished from other malignant pulmonary tumors and whose 
      biological behavior is as yet not fully understood. Primary undifferentiated 
      pleomorphic sarcoma was diagnosed in the right lung of a 66 year-old man, who has 
      survived over 11 years after treatment with endobronchial tumor debulking by 
      laser therapy and radiotherapy.
