AB  - The term "interventional pulmonology" (IP) supersedes the previously used term 
      "thoracic endoscopy," a change that reflects the evolution of a specialty devoted 
      to performing highly sophisticated and technologically advanced procedures in the 
      lungs and chest. Continuing advances in technology promise to further expand IP's 
      diagnostic and therapeutic frontiers. However, standardized educational programs 
      to train and test IP physicians will be essential to maintain a high standard of 
      practice in the field.
