TI  - [Primary bronchial plasmacytoma: computed tomography findings].
PG  - 504-7
LID - 10.1016/j.rx.2009.04.005 [doi]
AB  - Extramedullary plasmacytomas are malignant neoplasms of the plasmatic cells of 
      the soft tissues. Primary pulmonary plasmacytoma is the rarest type of 
      extramedullary plasmacytoma. The radiologic findings are unspecific and the 
      diagnosis is histologic. Chest CT is useful for confirming its location and 
      planning surgery. We present a case of primary endobronchial plasmacytoma in an 
      adult diagnosed at histology. We describe the findings at plain-film chest X-ray 
      and at CT, and we analyze the usefulness of 3D reconstructions for planning 
      surgery.
