TI  - [Cerebral arterial gas embolism as complication during the therapeutic 
      endobronchial use of argon plasma coagulation].
PG  - 353-4
LID - 10.1055/s-2008-1038133 [doi]
AB  - In this case report, argon plasma coagulation (APC) was applied in a male 
      individual to treat an occluding tumour of the right middle lobe bronchus with a 
      post-stenotic atelectasis. During attempted recanalisation, the patient suffered 
      a cerebral gas embolism as seen on CT scan, resulting in a distinct neurological 
      deficit. We discuss the available data about cerebral gas embolism as a 
      complication of APC and possibilities to avoid such complications.
