DP  - 2014 Jan
TI  - Pleomorphic adenoma presenting with a mediastinal mass.
PG  - 89-92
LID - 10.1111/1759-7714.12013 [doi]
AB  - Pleomorphic adenoma is the most common type of salivary gland tumor. Although it 
      rarely affects the trachea and bronchus, it usually grows in the airway and 
      presents as an endobronchial mass. We recently experienced a case of pleomorphic 
      adenoma originating in the bronchus and growing outward into the mediastinum. We 
      present this case with review of the computed tomography (CT) scan of the 
      patient's chest, the endoscopic ultrasound (EUS), and the histopathology report.
