TI  - Obstructive endo-bronchial pseudotumour due to herpes simplex type 2 infection in 
      an HIV-infected man.
PG  - 737-8
LID - 10.1258/ijsa.2009.008443 [doi]
AB  - We report a 31-year-old man with an obstructive bronchial lesion due to herpes 
      simplex type 2 infection, who responded promptly to endoscopic resection and oral 
      treatment with acyclovir. Exophytic lesions of the respiratory tract are rare, 
      potentially life-threatening, but readily treated complication of herpes simplex 
      virus infection in HIV-infected individuals.
