VI  - 62
IP  - 1
DP  - 2006 Feb
TI  - [Pulmonary mucormycosis. Two cases].
PG  - 37-42
AB  - Mucormycosis is a rare, devastating, opportunistic fungal infection, which occurs 
      principally in some particular conditions, specially in non-controlled diabetic 
      patients, notably during keratoacidosis. We report two cases in 62 and 72 
      year-old diabetic women. In both cases, histologic examination of endobronchial 
      biopsies showed tissue invasion by hyphae with characteristic morphology leading 
      to the diagnosis of pulmonary zygomycosis. This difficult diagnosis must be 
      evoked in diabetic patients with non-responsive lung infections in order to apply 
      early aggressive therapy.
