TI  - Epstein-Barr virus-associated bronchial leiomyoma in a boy with cellular 
      immunodeficiency.
PG  - 371-3
AB  - Bronchial leiomyoma is a rare disease in children. Recently, the association of 
      leiomyoma and HIV infection was reported. We describe a boy with a cellular 
      immunodeficiency, who had endobronchial leiomyoma. The tumor cells were positive 
      for Epstein-Barr virus-encoded RNA-1 (EBER-1) and Epstein-Barr virus-determined 
      nuclear antigen-2, suggesting a role of Epstein-Barr virus in the pathogenesis of 
      leiomyoma.
