DP  - 2009 Sep
TI  - [Disseminated cryptococcosis in an apparently immunocompetent patient].
PG  - 788-93
AB  - Cryptococcal infections occur frequently in immunocompromised patients 
      particularly in the context of AIDS, lymphomas and following immunosuppression 
      for organ transplant recipients. In these contexts the infection is readily 
      considered and diagnosis straightforward. The diagnosis is rarer and thus less 
      likely to be considered in immunocompetent patients which can lead to late 
      diagnosis and delay in initiation of therapy. We report the case of disseminated 
      cryptococcosis with endobronchial, cutaneous, bone and meningeal involvement in 
      an apparently immunocompetent patient. Before antifungal treatment could be 
      initiated the patient died of cerebral complications.
