TI  - [A case of a carcinoid tumour presenting as an "upper lobe syndrome"].
PG  - 1172-5
LID - 10.1016/j.rmr.2011.06.011 [doi]
AB  - A 53-year-old woman presented with progressive cough related to an endobronchial 
      carcinoid tumour. The location of the tumour in the right upper lobe bronchus 
      could be described as an "upper lobe syndrome" by analogy with the "middle lobe 
      syndrome" or Brock's syndrome. Surgical management consisted of lobectomy and 
      lymph node dissection. This established the diagnosis of typical carcinoid 
      tumour. There was no mediastinal nodal invasion. Three months after surgery all 
      symptoms had disappeared.
