TI  - [Three-year survival after treatment of a primary pulmonary angiosarcoma].
PG  - 55-8
AB  - We report an observation of angiosarcoma of the pulmonary artery in a 65-year-old 
      man hospitalized for acute dyspnea revealing a left mass hilaire which arose from 
      the pulmonary artery before the development of obstructive endobronchial 
      extension. The therapeutic sequence associated removal of the lobar bronchus 
      obstruction by interventional endoscopy, chemotherapy using 
      ifosfamide-doxorubicin, complete left pneumonectomy and auxiliary chemotherapy 
      with 2 additional cycles. The patient was free of tumor relapse at nearly 3 years 
      follow-up.
