TI  - [Pneumomediastinum and diffuse alveolar pain. Severe interstitial pneumopathy due 
      to dermatomyositis].
PG  - 76-9
LID - 10.1016/j.reuma.2008.09.002 [doi]
AB  - We have recently observed the case of a 36-year-old man with dermatomyositis of 
      recent onset, who developed masive pneumomediastinum and subcutaneous emphysema 
      at the onset of a progresive and severe pulmonary disease. Although there were no 
      sign of parenchymal cysts, after the bronchoscopy it was possible to observe 
      endobronchial necrotic injury which was considered as the likely source of the 
      air leak. He was treated with high dose of corticosteroids, cyclophosphamide and 
      cyclosporin A which resulted in the disappearance of the pneumomediastinum and 
      subcutaneous emphysema and the progressive improvement of both parenchymal lung 
      disease and respiratory insufficiency, enabled us to progressively taper the dose 
      of corticosteroids.
