VI  - 176
IP  - 45
DP  - 2014 Nov 3
TI  - [Surprising squamous cell carcinoma in the right upper lobe at bronchoscopy in a 
      heavy smoker].
LID - V05140262 [pii]
AB  - A 60-year-old male heavy smoker surprisingly presented with a squamous cell 
      carcinoma in the right upper lobe at bronchoscopy. Combined PET-CT classified the 
      lung cancer as T1aN0M0. However, the endoscopic classification was T2a, which 
      radically reversed the treatment schedule. CONCLUSIONS: 1) A careful bronchoscopy 
      is important even in cases where lung cancer is not expected. 2) Accurate 
      endobronchial classification can be crucial. 3) There is need for training 
      requirements to obtain a satisfactory level of competence in bronchoscopy.
