TI  - Teaching conventional transbronchial needle aspiration. A continuum.
PG  - 685-9
LID - 10.1513/AnnalsATS.201308-272ED [doi]
AB  - Proponents of the endobronchial ultrasound-guided transbronchial needle 
      aspiration (EBUS-TBNA) propose that in this era of EBUS-TBNA, training for 
      conventional transbronchial needle aspiration (C-TBNA) should be abandoned. The 
      authors of this editorial provide the opposing view. C-TBNA has a short and a 
      steep learning curve and adds to the diagnostic yield of flexible bronchoscopy in 
      a cost-effective fashion. Considering its simplicity, availability, 
      affordability, safety, and several unique indications, C-TBNA continues to 
      contribute to the welfare of patients worldwide. It should remain as an integral 
      part of pulmonary fellowship training programs.
