TI  - [Mucoepidermoid carcinoma in a 13-year-old girl; report of a case].
PG  - 423-6
AB  - A 13-year-old girl was referred to our hospital for chest pain and atelectasis of 
      left upper lobe on chest X-ray film. Bronchoscopy revealed an endobronchial tumor 
      obstructing left main bronchus. Left upper lobectomy with bronchoplasty was 
      performed. The tumor was a polyp 34 x 17 x 17 mm in size and obstructed left main 
      bronchus. Histologically the tumor was a low-grade malignant mucoepidermoid 
      carcinoma with malignant pleural effusin. The patient has been well and free of 
      recurrence for 8 years postoperatively.
