VI  - 41
IP  - 1
DP  - 2006 Jan
TI  - Endobronchial migration of prosthetic patch after congenital diaphragmatic hernia 
      repair.
PG  - e65-7
AB  - Surgical repair of congenital diaphragmatic hernia (CDH) can be performed by 
      means of either direct suturing of the diaphragm or positioning of a prosthetic 
      patch. However, half of all prosthetic patches show evidence of reherniation. We 
      describe the case of an 8-year-old girl who presented with prosthesis dislocation 
      and fistulization in the right lower bronchus as a complication of a CDH repair 
      that she underwent when she was 1 year old. Abdominal ultrasound and magnetic 
      resonance imaging suggested a hernia relapse, whereas chest computed tomographic 
      scan failed to identify the diaphragmatic defect. Only fibrobronchoscopy allowed 
      fistulization of the prosthesis into the bronchi to be correctly diagnosed.
