TI  - Photodynamic therapy: a case series demonstrating its role in patients receiving 
      mechanical ventilation.
PG  - 1419-23
AB  - Photodynamic therapy (PDT) has long been used to treat cancers within the 
      tracheobronchial tree. There have been many reports about the use of PDT for the 
      treatment of carcinoma in situ and for obstructive endobronchial lesions. PDT has 
      not been previously reported in patients receiving mechanical ventilation. PDT 
      offers the advantages of a relatively short duration of treatment, a low side 
      effect profile, and relatively low risk when compared to Nd-YAG laser in patients 
      receiving mechanical ventilation. We report the first successful use of PDT to 
      wean patients from mechanical ventilation.
