VI  - 43
IP  - 3
DP  - 2013 Mar
TI  - Inflammatory myofibroblastic tumor of the lung: a rare cause of atelectasis in 
      children.
PG  - 381-4
LID - 10.1007/s00247-012-2508-x [doi]
AB  - Although rare, inflammatory myofibroblastic tumor is the most common primary lung 
      mass in children. We report the case of an 11-year-old boy investigated for 
      persistent cough and dyspnea with complete left lung atelectasis mimicking 
      pneumonia. CT and MRI showed an endobronchial mass of the left main bronchus. The 
      boy underwent endoscopic resection of the tumor and histology was in favor of an 
      inflammatory myofibroblastic tumor of the lung. This diagnosis should be 
      suspected in children with recurrent pneumonia. The prognosis is good after 
      complete resection.
