TI  - Argon-plasma treatment in benign metastasizing leiomyoma of the lung: a case 
      report.
PG  - 921-3; discussion 925
AB  - Benign metastasizing leiomyomas of the lung are rare smooth muscle cells tumours. 
      We report the case of a 48 year-old female who was evaluated due to persistent 
      cough, progressive dyspnoea and constitutional symptoms. Chest computed 
      tomography revealed a left endobronchial mass, multiple parenchyma nodules and a 
      pleural effusion. Bronchial biopsy histological features were consistent with 
      benign metastasizing leiomyoma. The patient was successfully treated with 
      argon-plasma and mechanical debulking. There was no disease relapse in the last 
      four years.
