TI  - Topical mitomycin-C for obstructing endobronchial granuloma.
PG  - e22-3
AB  - An elderly woman with post-tuberculous stricture of the lower trachea and main 
      bronchi underwent laser re-canalization, balloon dilation, and silicone stent 
      insertion in the lower trachea and main bronchi. Subsequently she had recurrent 
      dyspnea develop due to obstructing granulomas, which necessitated four endoscopic 
      procedures in 2 years. The tracheal stent was removed and topical mitomycin-C was 
      applied using saturated pledgets at a dose of 0.5 mg/mL for 2 minutes each over 
      the lower trachea and both orifices of the main bronchi. Follow-up for 24 months 
      showed no recurrence of symptoms. Bronchoscopy and spirometry performed at 2, 6, 
      and 12 months showed resolution of the granulomas.
