DP  - 2006 Jun
TI  - Rapidly growing endobronchial hamartoma with bone marrow tissue.
PG  - 2287-9
AB  - A 29-year-old woman presented with a 4 x 3.5 cm circumscribed mass located in the 
      left upper lobe, which had not been detected in a chest roentgenogram that was 
      taken 3 years prior. Bone scintigraphy using technetium-99m methylene 
      diphosphonate revealed an increased uptake of the isotope in the mass, indicating 
      increased osteoplastic activity. She underwent surgical resection of the mass and 
      the pathologic diagnosis was endobronchially located pulmonary hamartoma, which 
      contained bone marrow tissue. An extremely rare case of pulmonary hamartoma 
      showing rapid growth and involving bone marrow tissue is presented.
