VI  - 52
IP  - 3
DP  - 2013
TI  - Bronchial fibroepithelial polyp: a case report and review of the literature.
PG  - 373-6
AB  - Fibroepithelial polyps of the bronchus are uncommon. We herein report a rare case 
      of a recurrent bronchial fibroepithelial polyp. A 61-year-old man was admitted to 
      the hospital due to recurrent pneumonia. Chest computed tomography showed 
      consolidation and atelectasis in the right lower lobe. Bronchoscopy revealed a 
      mobile polypoid tumor protruding from the right lower lobe bronchus. We performed 
      endobronchial resection, and a pathological examination revealed a 
      fibroepithelial polyp. However, surveillance bronchoscopy performed six months 
      after tumor resection detected a relapse. We herein report a case of a recurrent 
      bronchial fibroepithelial polyp and also review the relevant literature.
