DP  - 2008 May
TI  - Endotracheal metastasis from squamous cell cancer of the head and neck: PET/CT 
      imaging.
PG  - 340-1
LID - 10.1097/RLU.0b013e31816a790a [doi]
AB  - Lung cancer is the main malignancy with frequent endotracheal and endobronchial 
      dissemination. Extrapulmonary sources of airway metastasis are less common, 
      predominantly seen with breast, colorectal, and renal neoplasms. Head and neck 
      cancer represents only a small fraction of tumors with tracheal luminal 
      metastasis. We present 2 such rare cases with F-18 FDG PET/CT imaging. These 2 
      companion cases show in one instance an obvious hypermetabolic endotracheal 
      lesion and in the other one a discrete airway metastasis overlooked by chest CT 
      and diagnosed by PET with coregistered CT.
