IS  - 0007-0912 (Linking)
VI  - 94
IP  - 1
DP  - 2005 Jan
TI  - Experience with the Arndt paediatric bronchial blocker.
PG  - 92-4
AB  - Previously reported techniques for single lung ventilation in children have 
      failed to provide consistent, single lung ventilation with relative ease and 
      reliability. We report our experience with the use of a new device, the Arndt 5 
      French (Fr) paediatric endobronchial blocker, for single lung ventilation in a 
      series of 24 children. We were able to achieve single lung ventilation in 23 of 
      the 24 patients (aged 2-16 yr). Placement required approximately 5-15 min. 
      Attempts at placement were aborted in one patient who was unable to tolerate even 
      short periods of apnoea because of lung pathology. Although it has some 
      limitations, our experience suggests that the paediatric bronchial blocker can be 
      used as a consistent, safe method of single lung ventilation in most young 
      children.
