TI  - Combination of (18)-FDG and (68)Ga-DOTATOC PET-CT to differentiate endobronchial 
      carcinoids and inflammatory myofibroblastic tumors.
PG  - 272-4
LID - 10.4103/0022-3859.58932 [doi]
AB  - Bronchial masses in young patients are a diagnostic challenge as the signs and 
      symptoms are overlapping. Conventional radiological investigations reveal a mass 
      but are not diagnostic and biopsy remains the only means of preoperative 
      diagnosis. Functional imaging is now emerging as an important tool in the 
      evaluation of these patients and may have a potential to suggest a possible 
      diagnosis. A combination of (18) F-FDG PET-CT and (68) Ga-DOTATOC PET-CT scan is 
      one such example, which revealed contrasting findings in two patients that are 
      being presented here.
