TI  - A case of small cell lung cancer treated with chemoradiotherapy followed by 
      photodynamic therapy.
PG  - 637-9
LID - 10.1136/thx.2008.112912 [doi]
AB  - Here, we present the case of a 51-year-old man with limited-stage small cell lung 
      cancer (LS-SCLC) who received concurrent chemoradiotherapy and photodynamic 
      therapy (PDT). The patient was diagnosed as having LS-SCLC with an endobronchial 
      mass in the left main bronchus. Following concurrent chemoradiotherapy, a mass 
      remaining in the left lingular division was treated with PDT. Clinical and 
      histological data indicate that the patient has remained in complete response for 
      2 years without further treatment. This patient represents a rare case of 
      complete response in LS-SCLC treated with PDT.
