DP  - 2002
TI  - [Ways of overcoming drug resistance in patients with pulmonary tuberculosis].
PG  - 16-8
AB  - To elucidate the combined effect of surfactants and antituberculous drugs, the 
      surfactant myrastimine was tested. Two series of sputum cultures with 
      multidrug-resistant Mycobacterium tuberculosis (MBT) strains were made. The 
      experimental results confirmed that myramistine noticeably enhanced the 
      sensitivity of multidrug-resistant MBT strains to antituberculous agents. The use 
      of endobronchial and intracavernous myramistine in combination with 
      antituberculous agents to patients with destructive pulmonary tuberculosis caused 
      by multidrug-resistant MBT strains reduced the latter's resistance to 
      antibiotics, cured tubendobronchitis in most patients, created conditions for 
      obliteration of the cavernous cavity. Positive changes are noted in the first 4 
      months after the initiation of therapy, which can prepare patients for surgical 
      treatment more rapidly.
