DP  - 2000 Sep-Oct
TI  - Ultrastructural aspects of reactivity of regional lymph nodes on pulmonary 
      inflammation and following endobronchial laser therapy.
PG  - 311-7
AB  - The purpose of this study is the evaluation of reactivity of the regional lymph 
      nodes on infectious-destructive process in the lung, and the efficacy of 
      different therapeutical tactics. Examination of 7 regional lymph nodes from 7 
      patients with pulmonary inflammation showed marked manifestations of acute 
      lymphadenitis. Generally speaking, these lymph nodes were enlarged and manifested 
      signs of severe cell alteration and damaged processes of lymphocyte reproduction 
      and migration. In 10 lymph nodes from 10 patients with similar pulmonary 
      pathology receiving the same therapeutical measures combined with laser therapy 
      course, neither lymphadenitis nor cell alteration signs were found. The results 
      indicate the high plastic abilities of the lymph nodes and the efficacy of laser 
      biostimulation.
