DP  - 2004 Jul
TI  - Innovative approaches to lung volume reduction for emphysema.
PG  - 238-48
AB  - The 10 years of resurgent interest in lung volume reduction surgery (LVRS) and 
      recent National Emphysema Treatment Trial findings for emphysema have stimulated 
      a range of innovative alternative ideas aimed at improving outcomes and reducing 
      complications associated with current LVRS techniques. Concepts being actively 
      investigated at this time include surgical resection with compression/banding 
      devices, endobronchial blockers, sealants, obstructing devices and valves, and 
      bronchial bypass methods. These novel approaches are reaching the stage of 
      clinical trials at this time. Theory, design issues, methods, potential 
      advantages and limitations, and available results are presented. Extensive 
      research in the near future will help to determine the potential clinical 
      applicability of these new approaches to the treatment of emphysema symptoms.
