TI  - Left lower sleeve lobectomy by uniportal video-assisted thoracoscopic approach.
PG  - 237-9
LID - 10.1093/icvts/ivt441 [doi]
AB  - Endobronchial tumours requiring sleeve resection have been usually considered a 
      contraindication for video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery (VATS). However, with 
      new technical advances and the experience gained in VATS, sleeve lobectomy has 
      been performed by thoracoscopy in experienced VATS centres. Right-sided sleeve 
      anastomoses are easier to perform by VATS than left-sided ones because of the 
      presence of the pulmonary artery and aortic arch on the left side. Most surgeons 
      use a 3 to 4 incision VATS technique for sleeve anastomosis but the surgery can 
      be performed by using only one incision. This is the first report of a left-sided 
      sleeve lobectomy by uniportal approach.
